// REJECTS: Unexpected token '('. Valid alternatives: ['[']
//
// A function body is BRACES; the only thing that may appear between the return type and
// the body is a bracketed pre-constraint list, which is why '[' is the sole alternative
// offered.
//
// That single-element alternatives list is the fixture's real content. It proves the
// constraint block is positionally pinned between signature and body -- not floating
// anywhere in the declaration -- and it proves parens are not an accepted body form even
// though the function's own parameter list, three tokens earlier, is parens.
###Pure
function fixture::neg::parenBody(n: Integer[1]): Integer[1]
(
   $n * 2;
)
